{"study_accession":"PRJNA1162571","secondary_study_accession":"SRP533459","title":"Exploring the Landscape of Microproteins in T Cells: Insights Gained from Nascent Protein Profiling and Global Proteomics Approaches","description":"Microproteins, as hidden players in the proteomic club, are encoded by small open reading frames (sORFs) and have garnered increasing attention in recent years. T cells play a critical role in the immune system's response to cancer, however, the exploration of novel microproteins in T cells remains an unexplored area. In this study, we employed an integrated approach combined nascent protein profiling and quantitative global proteomics to identify novel microproteins in human T cells. Overall design: In brief, we isolated CD3+ T cells from human peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs). T cell activation was performed either with phorbol PMA 25 ng/mL and Iono 1 μg/mL or with anti-CD3/CD28-coated microbeads (ThermoFisher Scientific, #11161D) at a bead to cell ratio of 1: 1, at 37 °C with 5% CO2 for 24 hours. Then RNA-Seq data were acquired for inactivated T cells, activated T cells with PMA/Iono treatment, and activated T cells with anti-CD3/CD28 stimulate.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":9,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN43816651","study_accession":"PRJNA1162571","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Donor3, T cell, PMA/Ionomycin","description":"Donor3, T cell, PMA/Ionomycin","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8523950","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-09-27","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["cell_subtype","T cell"],["genotype","WT"],["treatment","PMA/Ionomycin"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR30716773","experiment_accession":"SRX26119974","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":55032537,"base_count":1650976110